Implement the attachment action menu for ChatPop so it behaves like a native iOS expanding quick-action menu.

IMPORTANT:
Do not redesign unrelated parts.
Only implement/refine the "+" attachment menu behavior and UI.

==================================================
1. TRIGGER BEHAVIOR
==================================================

When the user taps the "+" button inside the message composer:

- Open an attachment action menu from the bottom-left area near the "+" button
- The menu should expand vertically upward
- It should feel smooth, premium, and native to iOS
- The opening motion should clearly feel like it rises upward from the "+" trigger

When the user taps the close "X" button:

- The menu should collapse back downward
- It should animate down toward the bottom
- Do not instantly disappear
- The closing motion should feel like the menu is returning back to the original trigger area

==================================================
2. MENU ITEMS
==================================================

Show these four actions stacked vertically:

1. Camera
2. Photos
3. Audio
4. File

Each row should contain:
- a circular colored icon on the left
- a text label on the right

Use this order exactly:
Camera
Photos
Audio
File

==================================================
