==================================================

Below the vertical menu, show a circular "X" close button.

Behavior:
- tapping X closes the menu
- menu animates downward while closing
- the X should remain visually aligned with the menu system
- use a subtle dark circular button with white or light icon

==================================================
5. OPEN/CLOSE ANIMATION
==================================================

Opening:
- start near the "+" button
- expand upward item by item or as a smooth lifted stack
- each menu item can slightly fade + slide upward
- motion should feel lightweight and native

Closing:
- reverse the animation
- items slide/fold downward
- the stack collapses down smoothly
- no abrupt disappearance

Optional polish:
- slightly stagger the menu item appearance
- slightly blur/dim the background while the menu is open

==================================================
6. IOS FEEL
==================================================

Make the interaction feel like real iOS quality:

- smooth spring animation
- responsive tap states
- clean spacing
- clear typography
- no heavy or clunky animation

If there is an existing custom implementation, refine it rather than replacing unrelated composer logic.

==================================================
